  {
   "what": "acceptance.mjs, canary.sh, focus_replay.mjs, lint_js_test.sh, run_test.sh, batch_test.sh, private_names_test.sh, prepush_scan_test.sh, uber_seed_test.sh, uber_safe_directory_test.sh, lib_mutate.sh",
   "why": "verification surfaces: the campaign mutates the production behaviour they protect, not the tests themselves (mutation-testing.md)."
  },
  {
   "what": "tools/offline_lanes.sh",
   "why": "a measurement probe whose output a human reads; nothing is gated on it."
  },
  {
   "what": "uber.sh seed: the mktemp temp name, and the post-mv `[ -d registry ]` fallback",
   "why": "equivalent under the flock: only one seeder copies at a time, so a fixed temp name cannot collide, and its mv cannot meet an existing registry, so the fallback is never reached; the flock and the inner registry check are faults (ub-flock, ub-inner-guard), both killed by the copy-count case."
  },
  {
   "what": "private_names.sh: `--no-renames` on `git show`, and the `exclude=()` reset for an unconfigured remote",
   "why": "equivalent in the scan's own domain \u2014 commits the remote lacks, in pre-push mode or a --range starting at a published tip: the paths clause (diff-tree --no-renames) already names a rename's target, and a renamed file's other lines were scanned in the commit that added them; `--remotes=<url>` matches no tracking ref (a ref name cannot hold ':' or '..'), so the reset excludes nothing more. A --range starting at an UNPUBLISHED commit is outside that domain."
  },
  {
   "what": "generated bindings, the viewer bundle main.js, the visual manifest",
   "why": "projections: their generators are what is mutated."
  },
  {
   "what": "uber.sh seed: the outer `[ ! -d \"$CARGO_HOME/registry\" ]` guard",
   "why": "equivalent: under the flock the inner `[ -d \"$CARGO_HOME/registry\" ] && exit 0` already refuses to replace an existing registry, so the outer check only saves taking the lock; measured survivor, not a missing case."
  },
  {
   "what": "report_io.clj: the basename guard `(re-matches #\"[^/\\\\\\\\]{1,255}\" base)`",
   "why": "equivalent on a POSIX filesystem: the split on both separators leaves no separator in the basename, Clojure's split drops trailing empty strings, and a :file is attached only to an admission refusal of a file actually read, whose name the filesystem bounds at 255 bytes (NAME_MAX on Linux, 255 UTF-8 bytes on macOS APFS), hence at most 255 characters. Kept as insurance that the output satisfies the contract's regex; measured survivor."
  },
  {
   "what": "report.clj presentational CSS without a deterministic oracle: the patterned `.running` fill (--mark-run-a/b), `.selected-casing` width, the `aria-pressed` fill, `h2[tabindex='-1']:focus{outline:none}`",
   "why": "the contrast oracle counts patterned fills as skipped and nothing measures stroke width or a pressed fill, so no suite can judge them; they are judged by the Sonnet visual review, which CLAUDE.md says is not a gate verdict. Declared as unjudged, not as killed."
  },
  {
   "what": "lint_js.sh: `--network none` on the ESLint container",
   "why": "no observable effect today: ESLint with this config makes no network request, so no input distinguishes the flag's presence; it guards against a future plugin that would."
  },
  {
   "what": "lint.mk lanes, workflow steps and path filters, the hook's container block wiring",
   "why": "configuration, verified by the lanes running in CI and the hook, not by mutation."
  },
  {
   "what": "view/dom.cljs: the `\"g\"` entry in the svg tag enum",
   "why": "equivalent in every shipped page: the enum is a malli function schema, and only the JVM side instruments schemas (gate/diagnostic.clj); the browser bundle never does, so no browser run observes it. The casing layer the entry permits is faulted directly (vw-casing-layer)."
  }
 ]
